<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" ?><transcript><text start="3.76" dur="5.12">Mr. President, Amy Atkins mother has not</text><text start="6.56" dur="5.28">cared for her in about 50 years after</text><text start="8.88" dur="4.719">her stepdad was indicted for raping her.</text><text start="11.84" dur="3.04">Why should anyone listen to what the</text><text start="13.599" dur="3.041">mother has to say?</text><text start="14.88" dur="3.68">&amp;gt;&amp;gt; Well, I know nothing about it. All I</text><text start="16.64" dur="4.479">know is the mother said very bad things</text><text start="18.56" dur="6">about Actton, who I guess is running for</text><text start="21.119" dur="6.561">governor against Vake. And all I can say</text><text start="24.56" dur="5.039">is Vake is great. And I know one thing,</text><text start="27.68" dur="4.48">if my mother said bad about me, it would</text><text start="29.599" dur="5.12">be a major news story. That&amp;#39;s for sure.</text><text start="32.16" dur="4.64">So, I don&amp;#39;t know what it is, but I guess</text><text start="34.719" dur="4.561">the mother said very bad things about</text><text start="36.8" dur="4.72">the one who&amp;#39;s running for governor. And</text><text start="39.28" dur="4.24">I think you have to take that seriously.</text><text start="41.52" dur="3.76">&amp;gt;&amp;gt; Is there anything in a campaign ad that</text><text start="43.52" dur="3.6">should be off limits?</text><text start="45.28" dur="4.48">&amp;gt;&amp;gt; I know one thing, if my mother said that</text><text start="47.12" dur="4.88">about me, it would be uh you would have</text><text start="49.76" dur="4.479">hit gold. You would have been very happy</text><text start="52" dur="3.92">about it. So, I know nothing about it</text><text start="54.239" dur="4.401">other than the mother said horrible</text><text start="55.92" dur="5.6">things about a person that&amp;#39;s running for</text><text start="58.64" dur="5.44">governor of a great state, right? A</text><text start="61.52" dur="3.84">great state. And if it&amp;#39;s even a little</text><text start="64.08" dur="2.8">bit true, you don&amp;#39;t want her as</text><text start="65.36" dur="3.52">governor. So, I ask you about your</text><text start="66.88" dur="4.48">&amp;gt;&amp;gt; campaigning for Ashley Henson tonight in</text><text start="68.88" dur="4.239">Iowa. She said that the Rama Swami ad is</text><text start="71.36" dur="4.16">absolutely terrible and it should be</text><text start="73.119" dur="4.961">taken down. Why are you saying that&amp;#39;s</text><text start="75.52" dur="5.44">her opinion? I&amp;#39;m defending it because I</text><text start="78.08" dur="4.719">know that if that ad were about my</text><text start="80.96" dur="4">mother, you would love it. You would</text><text start="82.799" dur="4.481">love every inch of it. And what&amp;#39;s</text><text start="84.96" dur="4.4">happened is the press has teamed up</text><text start="87.28" dur="4">because he&amp;#39;s a Republican and they&amp;#39;ve</text><text start="89.36" dur="5.119">tried to make it like it&amp;#39;s a horrible</text><text start="91.28" dur="5.6">thing. This is a mother saying very bad</text><text start="94.479" dur="4.401">things about her daughter. And I don&amp;#39;t</text><text start="96.88" dur="4.96">know why that should be shielded. The</text><text start="98.88" dur="5.599">only problem is the press has decided to</text><text start="101.84" dur="5.44">unify and act like it&amp;#39;s a horrible</text><text start="104.479" dur="5.361">thing. It&amp;#39;s horrible for her. And I told</text><text start="107.28" dur="5.519">Vake, I said, &amp;quot;Well, if it were about</text><text start="109.84" dur="6.48">you or about especially about me, if</text><text start="112.799" dur="5.201">Mary Mloud, my mother, Mary Mloud, Trump</text><text start="116.32" dur="2.799">said that about me, you&amp;#39;d have it as</text><text start="118" dur="3.119">your number one story.&amp;quot;</text><text start="119.119" dur="3.921">&amp;gt;&amp;gt; On Ukraine, Mr. President, President</text><text start="121.119" dur="3.841">Zalinski said these new Russian strikes</text><text start="123.04" dur="3.52">overnight are proof that nothing&amp;#39;s</text><text start="124.96" dur="2.88">changed with Putin, that he doesn&amp;#39;t want</text><text start="126.56" dur="2.8">peace. How do you see it?</text><text start="127.84" dur="3.44">&amp;gt;&amp;gt; Well, we&amp;#39;ll see how it works out. That&amp;#39;s</text><text start="129.36" dur="4.32">been happening a lot. Mr. President,</text><text start="131.28" dur="4.4">what a mistake Barack Obama is coming to</text><text start="133.68" dur="3.84">Michigan right before you go through</text><text start="135.68" dur="2.96">Michigan. Any thoughts on how that&amp;#39;s</text><text start="137.52" dur="3.359">going to work out for Democrats?</text><text start="138.64" dur="4.16">&amp;gt;&amp;gt; Well, I won Michigan by a lot. It was a</text><text start="140.879" dur="3.601">It&amp;#39;s a great state. I&amp;#39;ve done a lot for</text><text start="142.8" dur="3.76">them, the Air Force base and everything</text><text start="144.48" dur="3.6">else. And I think we&amp;#39;re going to do very</text><text start="146.56" dur="3.44">well in Michigan. I really do.</text><text start="148.08" dur="4.239">&amp;gt;&amp;gt; And then you saw what Elon Omar said</text><text start="150" dur="4.64">about her brother. She was asked if</text><text start="152.319" dur="4.401">she&amp;#39;d married her brother and she said,</text><text start="154.64" dur="3.84">&amp;quot;Not to my knowledge.&amp;quot; Why do you think</text><text start="156.72" dur="3.44">that she didn&amp;#39;t just say no? Well, if</text><text start="158.48" dur="4.64">you asked me that same question about,</text><text start="160.16" dur="5.6">let&amp;#39;s say, my sister, I would say no.</text><text start="163.12" dur="5.44">She said not to my knowledge. Uh, that</text><text start="165.76" dur="4.72">tells you a lot right there. No, she&amp;#39;s</text><text start="168.56" dur="3.36">I&amp;#39;ve never been a big fan of hers. I</text><text start="170.48" dur="4.32">I&amp;#39;ll be honest. Let&amp;#39;s see how it all</text><text start="171.92" dur="4.16">works out. But that statement tells you</text><text start="174.8" dur="3.76">a lot.</text><text start="176.08" dur="4.32">&amp;gt;&amp;gt; Could you call Elon Musk to bring back</text><text start="178.56" dur="6.56">Stling for Ukraine? Well, I don&amp;#39;t want</text><text start="180.4" dur="6.8">to say, but uh I know it was a very</text><text start="185.12" dur="4.72">interesting situation, so I don&amp;#39;t want</text><text start="187.2" dur="5.039">to comment one way or the other, but uh</text><text start="189.84" dur="4.399">&amp;gt;&amp;gt; the Wall Street my relationship with</text><text start="192.239" dur="3.441">Elon is a very good one. Go ahead.</text><text start="194.239" dur="3.28">&amp;gt;&amp;gt; The Wall Street Journal is reporting</text><text start="195.68" dur="3.199">that you called him and asked him to</text><text start="197.519" dur="3.521">&amp;gt;&amp;gt; I don&amp;#39;t want to comment on it. You know,</text><text start="198.879" dur="3.921">whether I called or whether somebody</text><text start="201.04" dur="4.16">else called doesn&amp;#39;t make any difference.</text><text start="202.8" dur="4.56">I guess the bottom line, he put it back.</text><text start="205.2" dur="5.36">&amp;gt;&amp;gt; Was it a mistake for Stormfield to be</text><text start="207.36" dur="4.64">slow down? Any</text><text start="210.56" dur="2.16">other question? Go ahead.</text><text start="212" dur="1.44">&amp;gt;&amp;gt; Thank you.</text><text start="212.72" dur="2.64">&amp;gt;&amp;gt; Say hello.</text><text start="213.44" dur="3.6">&amp;gt;&amp;gt; Thank you.</text><text start="215.36" dur="3.92">&amp;gt;&amp;gt; North Carolina question. Hi.</text><text start="217.04" dur="5.199">&amp;gt;&amp;gt; On June, you said at the recent rally</text><text start="219.28" dur="5.36">that you would order the DOJ to settle</text><text start="222.239" dur="4.241">those lawsuits if they&amp;#39;re legitimate.</text><text start="224.64" dur="3.84">Yeah. Why not do so now, sir?</text><text start="226.48" dur="3.44">&amp;gt;&amp;gt; Uh I think if they can do it reasonably,</text><text start="228.48" dur="4.16">they should settle. If they can&amp;#39;t, they</text><text start="229.92" dur="4.399">have to just go. But uh we want to take</text><text start="232.64" dur="4.159">care of a lot of soldiers. If the</text><text start="234.319" dur="4.881">soldiers were affected and it was it was</text><text start="236.799" dur="4.08">a proper situation, we want to take care</text><text start="239.2" dur="2.48">of it. We want to take care of our</text><text start="240.879" dur="2.56">soldiers.</text><text start="241.68" dur="3.759">&amp;gt;&amp;gt; You said it&amp;#39;s dependent on the midterms</text><text start="243.439" dur="3.601">results though. Uh why?</text><text start="245.439" dur="2.961">&amp;gt;&amp;gt; Well, because if we&amp;#39;re not there, then</text><text start="247.04" dur="3.36">somebody else is going to have to settle</text><text start="248.4" dur="4.88">it. So, I can&amp;#39;t speak for another</text><text start="250.4" dur="4.399">administration. So, uh, if we do badly</text><text start="253.28" dur="3.84">or if the people that we need</text><text start="254.799" dur="3.921">surrounding us can&amp;#39;t get it done because</text><text start="257.12" dur="3.679">you have a lot of congressmen up, you</text><text start="258.72" dur="3.919">have a lot of senators up, you have a</text><text start="260.799" dur="5.041">lot of people involved in that whole</text><text start="262.639" dur="5.681">situation. Uh, so if the Republicans</text><text start="265.84" dur="5.12">don&amp;#39;t do well, I I would say that maybe</text><text start="268.32" dur="4.64">they won&amp;#39;t get their money.</text><text start="270.96" dur="4.32">&amp;gt;&amp;gt; Why did you make no mention of the</text><text start="272.96" dur="4.239">sexual abuse allegations that Amy Actton</text><text start="275.28" dur="3.359">made against her stepfather who stayed</text><text start="277.199" dur="3.361">married to her mother?</text><text start="278.639" dur="3.84">&amp;gt;&amp;gt; Well, I have no idea. I don&amp;#39;t know the</text><text start="280.56" dur="4.4">mother. I don&amp;#39;t know her. I never heard</text><text start="282.479" dur="4.641">of her until just recently as somebody</text><text start="284.96" dur="5.04">running for governor of Ohio. I can tell</text><text start="287.12" dur="4.56">you this. If my mother ever made those</text><text start="290" dur="3.36">statements, I have a mother I had a</text><text start="291.68" dur="4.72">mother who&amp;#39;s up there right now looking</text><text start="293.36" dur="5.119">down. Mary Mloud Trump. If she ever made</text><text start="296.4" dur="4.72">statements like that about me, you and</text><text start="298.479" dur="4.401">your fake station would have it front</text><text start="301.12" dur="5.28">row center. You&amp;#39;d love it. What&amp;#39;s</text><text start="302.88" dur="5.759">happened is the the press has ganged up</text><text start="306.4" dur="4.4">on a woman making a horrible statement</text><text start="308.639" dur="3.921">about her daughter. And I don&amp;#39;t know why</text><text start="310.8" dur="3.52">she should be shielded or the daughter</text><text start="312.56" dur="2.479">should be sher stepmother a child</text><text start="314.32" dur="2.879">rapist.</text><text start="315.039" dur="5.121">&amp;gt;&amp;gt; Mother made a horrible statement about</text><text start="317.199" dur="4.641">the daughter said she was a dirty liar.</text><text start="320.16" dur="3.68">She said she was a lot of different</text><text start="321.84" dur="4.639">things and I don&amp;#39;t know why you&amp;#39;re not</text><text start="323.84" dur="5.44">allowed to say that she I know one</text><text start="326.479" dur="5.121">thing. If my mother who loved me made</text><text start="329.28" dur="4.24">those different you&amp;#39;d be the first one</text><text start="331.6" dur="4.159">to be broadcasting and you would have</text><text start="333.52" dur="4.48">found nothing wrong with him. Amy</text><text start="335.759" dur="4.801">Actton&amp;#39;s mother said horrible things</text><text start="338" dur="4.16">about Amy Actton. And I don&amp;#39;t know why</text><text start="340.56" dur="3.44">you&amp;#39;re not allowed to do that. You&amp;#39;re</text><text start="342.16" dur="5.039">not allowed to broadcast it. Now, I&amp;#39;ll</text><text start="344" dur="5.84">say this. The press has ganged up</text><text start="347.199" dur="5.84">because you hate it. Because that one ad</text><text start="349.84" dur="5.28">should really win. Look, if what the</text><text start="353.039" dur="4.481">mother said about the daughter is half</text><text start="355.12" dur="3.76">right, she has no right even running for</text><text start="357.52" dur="3.2">the governor of Ohio.</text><text start="358.88" dur="2.64">&amp;gt;&amp;gt; What about the daughter said about her</text><text start="360.72" dur="2.08">mother?</text><text start="361.52" dur="1.92">&amp;gt;&amp;gt; I don&amp;#39;t know what the daughter said. I</text><text start="362.8" dur="2.32">don&amp;#39;t know.</text><text start="363.44" dur="3.199">&amp;gt;&amp;gt; Her stepmother. Her mother remained</text><text start="365.12" dur="3.199">married to her stepfather who sexually</text><text start="366.639" dur="3.201">abused her when she was 12 years old.</text><text start="368.319" dur="1.841">&amp;gt;&amp;gt; When did she make that statement? Was it</text><text start="369.84" dur="2.16">just</text><text start="370.16" dur="3.36">&amp;gt;&amp;gt; in the 1970s?</text><text start="372" dur="3.919">They he was charged. Mr.</text><text start="373.52" dur="4.799">&amp;gt;&amp;gt; You know, I have no idea. All I know is</text><text start="375.919" dur="4.72">Amy Actton&amp;#39;s mother said horrible things</text><text start="378.319" dur="5.201">about Amy Actton, calling her a liar and</text><text start="380.639" dur="6.241">other things and unreliable, a lot of</text><text start="383.52" dur="5.679">very bad things. And I say that she&amp;#39;s</text><text start="386.88" dur="4.4">fair game. And I know one thing, if it</text><text start="389.199" dur="4.081">were my mother, I&amp;#39;d be fair game. And</text><text start="391.28" dur="4.96">you know that and you know that well.</text><text start="393.28" dur="5.28">You&amp;#39;re trying to help Amy Actton get</text><text start="396.24" dur="4.64">elected. The press has teamed up to help</text><text start="398.56" dur="4.56">Amy Actton get elected and that&amp;#39;s all it</text><text start="400.88" dur="4.4">is. What the mother said is terrible</text><text start="403.12" dur="3.84">from the standpoint that I wouldn&amp;#39;t want</text><text start="405.28" dur="3.759">somebody like that to be the governor of</text><text start="406.96" dur="4.56">a great state.</text><text start="409.039" dur="4.481">&amp;gt;&amp;gt; There are a lot of races in red states,</text><text start="411.52" dur="5.2">Mr. President. There are a lot of close</text><text start="413.52" dur="3.76">races in red states. Why are Democrats</text><text start="416.72" dur="2.08">doing so well?</text><text start="417.28" dur="4.56">&amp;gt;&amp;gt; I don&amp;#39;t know if they&amp;#39;re close. I mean, I</text><text start="418.8" dur="7.6">just saw that the New York Times</text><text start="421.84" dur="6.079">used the poll numbers of a totally fake,</text><text start="426.4" dur="5.12">you know, a group that said they were</text><text start="427.919" dur="7.761">fake numbers against me. So, I don&amp;#39;t</text><text start="431.52" dur="7.28">know if you saw that the New York Times,</text><text start="435.68" dur="4.799">the New York Times used fake poll</text><text start="438.8" dur="4.72">numbers against me and it was just</text><text start="440.479" dur="5.761">revealed. The polling company just said</text><text start="443.52" dur="4.56">that the numbers were fake. And I</text><text start="446.24" dur="4.16">haven&amp;#39;t had an apology from the New York</text><text start="448.08" dur="6">Times, but if you saw that polling</text><text start="450.4" dur="6.16">company, it was a fake poll. And the New</text><text start="454.08" dur="4.64">York Times uses that polling company.</text><text start="456.56" dur="4.96">So, to the best of my knowledge, they</text><text start="458.72" dur="4.08">have not apologized to me.</text><text start="461.52" dur="2.64">&amp;gt;&amp;gt; Are you going to be able to keep the</text><text start="462.8" dur="3.44">House and the Senate?</text><text start="464.16" dur="4.159">&amp;gt;&amp;gt; I hope so. I mean, we&amp;#39;ll see.</text><text start="466.24" dur="5.2">&amp;gt;&amp;gt; Look, we&amp;#39;ll see. When I run, we get</text><text start="468.319" dur="5.44">almost 50% more voters. So, if I can get</text><text start="471.44" dur="4.72">my voters out, we&amp;#39;re going to win. If we</text><text start="473.759" dur="6.241">can&amp;#39;t get the voters out, I guess not.</text><text start="476.16" dur="5.92">Uh, typically the the president of, you</text><text start="480" dur="5.039">know, Republican, Democrat, whatever,</text><text start="482.08" dur="5.04">doesn&amp;#39;t do well at midterms. I say this,</text><text start="485.039" dur="4.641">if my poll, if my people come out, even</text><text start="487.12" dur="6.56">a little bit will do great. But I think</text><text start="489.68" dur="6.16">the number is 49 or 50 50%. So, when I</text><text start="493.68" dur="4.48">run, 50% more people come out. I guess</text><text start="495.84" dur="5.039">that&amp;#39;s a compliment. I&amp;#39;d like to see if</text><text start="498.16" dur="4.56">I could get a lot of them out. Now, if</text><text start="500.879" dur="2.72">we do that, we&amp;#39;ll win easily in a</text><text start="502.72" dur="2.479">landslide.</text><text start="503.599" dur="2.88">&amp;gt;&amp;gt; Mr. President, question on Maine.</text><text start="505.199" dur="2.961">Question on Maine. You&amp;#39;re you&amp;#39;re going</text><text start="506.479" dur="3.361">all over the country. Do you have plans</text><text start="508.16" dur="3.439">to go to Maine? Would that help?</text><text start="509.84" dur="3.199">&amp;gt;&amp;gt; We&amp;#39;re going to go for a number. We&amp;#39;re</text><text start="511.599" dur="3.041">probably going to add a couple. It&amp;#39;s a</text><text start="513.039" dur="4.24">lot of work. I will tell you this is a</text><text start="514.64" dur="4.16">lot of this is a lot of travel, but I</text><text start="517.279" dur="4.161">love the people. We&amp;#39;re getting great</text><text start="518.8" dur="4.719">crowds. They have a line in Iowa that&amp;#39;s</text><text start="521.44" dur="4.72">miles long right now trying to get into</text><text start="523.519" dur="4.721">the arena.</text><text start="526.16" dur="4">time of Texas. You&amp;#39;re spending a lot of</text><text start="528.24" dur="2.88">money in time in Texas. I think the most</text><text start="530.16" dur="3.28">amount of money you&amp;#39;re spending</text><text start="531.12" dur="4.399">&amp;gt;&amp;gt; Well, I think this I think that uh we</text><text start="533.44" dur="5.12">have the greatest attorney general</text><text start="535.519" dur="4.721">running in the history of Texas and he&amp;#39;s</text><text start="538.56" dur="3.44">running against a guy they call him a</text><text start="540.24" dur="4.4">freak. I mean, that&amp;#39;s his nickname. He</text><text start="542" dur="4.16">is a freak. And Texas cannot have</text><text start="544.64" dur="3.68">Telefo.</text><text start="546.16" dur="4.239">So, what Texas has is the greatest</text><text start="548.32" dur="4.079">attorney general in their history and</text><text start="550.399" dur="3.921">one of the greatest attorney generals in</text><text start="552.399" dur="4.081">the country. And that&amp;#39;s what you want</text><text start="554.32" dur="3.44">for your senator.</text><text start="556.48" dur="4.16">&amp;gt;&amp;gt; Do you have any re do you have any</text><text start="557.76" dur="4.96">reaction to the reports that the the DOJ</text><text start="560.64" dur="3.44">is looking at Cory Luwendowski now?</text><text start="562.72" dur="2.96">&amp;gt;&amp;gt; I don&amp;#39;t know about it. I mean, I heard</text><text start="564.08" dur="4.319">something about it, but I don&amp;#39;t know</text><text start="565.68" dur="4.64">exactly what it is. All I know is I want</text><text start="568.399" dur="3.601">my people to be honest and if they&amp;#39;re</text><text start="570.32" dur="3.519">not going to be honest, they have to be</text><text start="572" dur="4.16">prosecuted. I don&amp;#39;t know about</text><text start="573.839" dur="3.841">specifically, but because I view if</text><text start="576.16" dur="4">people are not honest, they&amp;#39;re stealing</text><text start="577.68" dur="4.64">from me as president. They&amp;#39;re stealing</text><text start="580.16" dur="4.16">from me. So, I want my people to be</text><text start="582.32" dur="4.32">honest, and if they&amp;#39;re not honest, I&amp;#39;ll</text><text start="584.32" dur="2.8">have my DOJ go and do whatever they have</text><text start="586.64" dur="1.44">to do.</text><text start="587.12" dur="2">&amp;gt;&amp;gt; Don&amp;#39;t think you&amp;#39;re okay with that</text><text start="588.08" dur="3.439">investigation, Andrew?</text><text start="589.12" dur="4">&amp;gt;&amp;gt; I Well, I I could I guess I can stop</text><text start="591.519" dur="3.841">anything. Look,</text><text start="593.12" dur="3.92">&amp;gt;&amp;gt; if my people are not I have no idea what</text><text start="595.36" dur="3.599">he did. I have just heard about it a</text><text start="597.04" dur="4.16">little while. I want the people that</text><text start="598.959" dur="3.44">work for this administration to be 100%</text><text start="601.2" dur="2.96">honest.</text><text start="602.399" dur="5.041">&amp;gt;&amp;gt; How mean, Mr. President,</text><text start="604.16" dur="6.72">&amp;gt;&amp;gt; how Means resigned today from HHS is</text><text start="607.44" dur="6.399">Baja dead, sir.</text><text start="610.88" dur="6">Uh, don&amp;#39;t know her very well at all. I</text><text start="613.839" dur="3.521">guess you&amp;#39;re talking about it&amp;#39;s a Bobby</text><text start="616.88" dur="1.92">Kennedy.</text><text start="617.36" dur="4.24">&amp;gt;&amp;gt; Well, you&amp;#39;ll have to don&amp;#39;t know. It&amp;#39;s</text><text start="618.8" dur="4.479">doing great. Baja is doing great.</text><text start="621.6" dur="3.12">&amp;gt;&amp;gt; It sounds like you&amp;#39;re talking about him</text><text start="623.279" dur="3.041">specifically when you&amp;#39;re talking about</text><text start="624.72" dur="4.32">people stealing.</text><text start="626.32" dur="5.12">&amp;gt;&amp;gt; Uh, I would say this. If somebody is</text><text start="629.04" dur="4.56">dishonest, I consider them not only</text><text start="631.44" dur="5.12">against the country, I consider that</text><text start="633.6" dur="5.44">dishonest against me. So, I will never I</text><text start="636.56" dur="4.56">will never do anything to stop a</text><text start="639.04" dur="2.96">prosecution if somebody is dishonest.</text><text start="641.12" dur="2.159">Yep.</text><text start="642" dur="2.8">&amp;gt;&amp;gt; How worried are you about the</text><text start="643.279" dur="2.081">Mississippi Senate race? Why are you</text><text start="644.8" dur="2.24">going to Mississippi?</text><text start="645.36" dur="3.44">&amp;gt;&amp;gt; I&amp;#39;m just hearing about it now from you.</text><text start="647.04" dur="3.28">What What&amp;#39;s wrong with Mississippi?</text><text start="648.8" dur="2.8">&amp;gt;&amp;gt; Are you worried about losing the seat</text><text start="650.32" dur="3.199">there?</text><text start="651.6" dur="4.479">&amp;gt;&amp;gt; What are the poll numbers?</text><text start="653.519" dur="3.76">&amp;gt;&amp;gt; What are the pollith</text><text start="656.079" dur="1.921">&amp;gt;&amp;gt; and what is it? What are the poll</text><text start="657.279" dur="1.921">numbers?</text><text start="658" dur="3.36">&amp;gt;&amp;gt; It&amp;#39;s tough to say, but they&amp;#39;re</text><text start="659.2" dur="3.52">&amp;gt;&amp;gt; I mean, Cindy Hyde&amp;#39;s been very popular.</text><text start="661.36" dur="3.28">If I need to, you know, I went</text><text start="662.72" dur="5.04">Mississippi as like I did just about</text><text start="664.64" dur="5.04">everything else in a landslide. So, if I</text><text start="667.76" dur="4.24">need to get her over the top, I would go</text><text start="669.68" dur="4.96">there. She&amp;#39;s great. Cindy Hyde Smith is</text><text start="672" dur="4.959">great. So, if I need to go, I mean, I&amp;#39;m</text><text start="674.64" dur="3.759">pretty well booked up as you see, but if</text><text start="676.959" dur="3.361">I need to go, I&amp;#39;d go.</text><text start="678.399" dur="4.161">&amp;gt;&amp;gt; Sir, will you only endorse Vice</text><text start="680.32" dur="4.32">President Vance if Republicans hold the</text><text start="682.56" dur="2.88">majorities?</text><text start="684.64" dur="2.56">Vice President,</text><text start="685.44" dur="4.399">&amp;gt;&amp;gt; if Republicans don&amp;#39;t hold the</text><text start="687.2" dur="4.4">majorities, are you not going to endorse</text><text start="689.839" dur="2.961">Vice President Vance for 2028?</text><text start="691.6" dur="4">&amp;gt;&amp;gt; Where do you get that idea?</text><text start="692.8" dur="3.36">&amp;gt;&amp;gt; Well, you&amp;#39;ve just said it&amp;#39;s never</text><text start="695.6" dur="2.32">happens.</text><text start="696.16" dur="3.919">&amp;gt;&amp;gt; I never even thought of it. No, because</text><text start="697.92" dur="4">we&amp;#39;re just too we have too much time to</text><text start="700.079" dur="2.481">be thinking about that. It&amp;#39;s a long way</text><text start="701.92" dur="3.2">off.</text><text start="702.56" dur="4.56">&amp;gt;&amp;gt; Where will you Todd Has Todd Blanch</text><text start="705.12" dur="2.48">briefed you about the Corin Luendowski</text><text start="707.12" dur="2.08">situation?</text><text start="707.6" dur="3.76">&amp;gt;&amp;gt; No, he hasn&amp;#39;t. I just heard about it a</text><text start="709.2" dur="3.84">little while ago. But I want my people</text><text start="711.36" dur="3.2">to be honest. If he&amp;#39;s honest, that&amp;#39;s</text><text start="713.04" dur="2.479">good. If he&amp;#39;s not honest, you have to</text><text start="714.56" dur="2.719">pay a price.</text><text start="715.519" dur="4.081">&amp;gt;&amp;gt; And in all these tight races, Mr.</text><text start="717.279" dur="4">President, how do you think the Iran war</text><text start="719.6" dur="3.44">has impacted the races?</text><text start="721.279" dur="3.201">&amp;gt;&amp;gt; Well, in one way, they love it because</text><text start="723.04" dur="3.28">I&amp;#39;m doing what should have been done by</text><text start="724.48" dur="4.56">other presidents. In another way, maybe</text><text start="726.32" dur="5.28">they don&amp;#39;t. It&amp;#39;s there&amp;#39;s a price to pay,</text><text start="729.04" dur="4.32">which I knew immediately when I did it.</text><text start="731.6" dur="3.679">But we can&amp;#39;t let Iran have a nuclear</text><text start="733.36" dur="4.719">weapon. I mean, in one way, people</text><text start="735.279" dur="5.36">probably don&amp;#39;t love it, but many people,</text><text start="738.079" dur="4.241">many great patriots really love it. This</text><text start="740.639" dur="4">should have been done a long time ago by</text><text start="742.32" dur="4.48">other presidents, the Iran war, and</text><text start="744.639" dur="3.76">we&amp;#39;ve knocked the hell out of them. And</text><text start="746.8" dur="3.36">we may do it a little bit further. Thank</text><text start="748.399" dur="5.841">you, Mr. President. Was it a mistake to</text><text start="750.16" dur="4.08">slow down the battlefield over Ukraine?</text></transcript>